# What GitHub Linguist needs to know about Kest, in the shape its own
# `languages.yml` wants. The grammar it points at is `editors/vscode`, which is
# the one this project maintains; there is no second grammar, because two
# grammars are two answers about what a file looks like.
#
# `language_id` is left out on purpose and upstream's own instructions say to
# leave it out: `script/update-ids` generates it when the entry is added. It is
# theirs to give and not this project's to write down.
#
# Rehearsed against upstream on 2026-09-19, at linguist ee4fb24, and everything
# that can be done from here passed. See D1019:
#
#   this entry inserted in `lib/linguist/languages.yml`, alphabetically
#   `script/update-ids --check` names Kest as the one missing an ID
#   `script/update-ids` gives it one
#   `script/add-grammar https://github.com/Rawframe-Project/kest` registers the
#     submodule, runs upstream's grammar compiler over the grammar, finds no
#     problems, and writes `source.kest` into `grammars.yml`
#   `test/test_language.rb` is exactly as green with this entry as without it
#   `test/test_samples.rb` and `test/test_classifier.rb` pass
#   a `.kest` file in `samples/Kest` classifies as Kest
#
# What remains is not technical: upstream requires the extension to be in
# wide-spread use on public GitHub, assessed by search, and Kest is one
# repository. Nothing here fakes that and no pull request has been opened.
#
# Samples for the submission are the tree's own examples, which are real
# programs that run rather than files written to be counted. They are this
# project's own work under the MIT licence the repository carries:
#   examples/colony.kest    a world kept and worked on
#   examples/ants.kest      a frame over an array of value structs
#   examples/registry.kest  a store and references outside a game
#   lib/std/table.kest      a hash table written in the language
Kest:
  type: programming
  color: "#2f6f4e"
  extensions:
    - ".kest"
  tm_scope: source.kest
  ace_mode: text
  codemirror_mode: null
  interpreters:
    - kest
